---
import ChickuboInfoLayout from '@/layouts/ChickuboInfoLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<ChickuboInfoLayout title="Terms of Service" description="Terms for playing Chickubo: Cozy Chicken Farm, local progress, virtual items, and optional store purchases." icon="📜" updated>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <p>Chickubo is a cozy farming game for personal entertainment. Farm progress saves on the device, with optional Apple/iCloud synchronization on supported iOS builds. Optional virtual-item purchases, when available, are subject to the platform store's terms and your rights under applicable law.</p>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>Using Chickubo</h2>
    <p>These terms apply to Chickubo: Cozy Chicken Farm by NekoCode. On the title screen, check the agreement and select Play to accept these terms and acknowledge the Privacy Policy. Opening either document alone does not record agreement. You may use it for lawful, personal, non-commercial entertainment. If you are a minor, a parent or guardian should review these terms and authorize any purchases. Contact NekoCode at <a href="mailto:nekocode.dev@gmail.com?subject=Chickubo%20Terms">nekocode.dev@gmail.com</a> about these terms.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Game content and conduct</h2>
    <p>The game includes caring for hens, collecting eggs, growing crops, upgrades, and virtual rewards. Game artwork, characters, music, design, and software belong to their respective rights holders and are protected by applicable intellectual-property rights. You receive permission to play the game, not ownership of its content. Third-party license notices continue to apply.</p>
    <p>Do not use the game unlawfully, interfere with its operation, compromise purchase systems, or exploit errors to obtain unauthorized paid rewards. Nothing in these terms limits uses permitted by applicable law.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Device and iCloud saves</h2>
    <p>The game saves progress on your device. Supported, configured iOS builds can automatically sync a private encrypted snapshot through the current Apple/iCloud account. Native iCloud integration is undergoing validation; the in-game save screen shows availability. Settings → iCloud Save offers sync status, pause, conflict choices, and cloud deletion. Sync requires internet, iCloud access, and available storage. It is not immediate or guaranteed. Changes made on multiple devices may require you to choose a farm and are not merged. Purchase sign-in is separate from iCloud save ownership. Uninstalling, clearing app data, device failure, or changing devices may result in lost progress. Contact support before resetting the game if you have a save problem; recovery is not guaranteed.</p>
    <p>Offline progress is capped at eight hours and depends on supplies, capacity, and game production limits. Features and game balance may change in updates. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Optional purchase account</h2>
    <p>Core farm gameplay does not require an account. Optional purchase accounts and paid checkout are disabled in the current build. When available, paid purchases require an account authenticated with a code sent to your email address. Use an email address you control and protect your sign-in codes and device. Purchase verification associates purchases with the original account; an account is not a transferable farm or wallet.</p>
    <p>A purchase account does not provide farm backup, cross-device farm synchronization, or restoration of spent consumables. On supported iOS builds, separate Apple/iCloud sync can copy the saved farm snapshot, including its balances; it does not create new purchased items or a server-managed wallet. Signing out or requesting account deletion keeps the local farm and may keep local records linking purchases to their original account. When account services are available, initiate deletion in Settings → Purchases &amp; Account → Delete account after confirming. An accepted request disables purchases while provider removal may still be pending; it may prevent unfinished purchases from being delivered and does not cancel an Apple transaction or automatically request a refund. The <a href={`${base}apps/chickubo/privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a> describes the information removed and limited security records retained.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Optional purchases and virtual items</h2>
    <p>Paid checkout is not enabled in the current build. When optional purchases become available, review the product description and localized store price before confirming. Apple or the relevant platform store handles checkout under its own terms.</p>
    <p>Where available, optional store purchases provide consumable coins, gems, or a Farm Starter bundle. Chickubo does not currently offer an auto-renewing subscription. Product availability and eligibility are shown before purchase; a one-time offer is not a promise of another reward after reinstalling or resetting the game. Farm Starter is limited to one verified claim per purchase account. A previously authorized purchase awaiting store approval may be fulfilled after the displayed offer window ends; this does not create another offer or reward.</p>
    <p>Coins, gems, chickens, and other virtual items are for use within Chickubo. Purchased in-game currency does not expire. Virtual items are not money, have no cash-redemption value, and cannot be transferred or sold outside the game. Consumable items that have been delivered and used are not restored as new items. Checking unfinished transactions does not grant a second copy of a delivered reward. Refund eligibility is determined by applicable law and the store's policies; these terms do not remove your statutory rights.</p>
    <p>Where a random reward feature uses virtual currency, review its displayed probabilities, cost, and confirmation before spending. Rewards are virtual game items with no cash-redemption value. Hatchery egg recipes and incubation timers are separate from random rewards. For missing purchases, keep the store receipt and contact <a href={`${base}apps/chickubo/support/`}>Chickubo Support</a>. Apple refund requests can be made through <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Report a Problem</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Apple's license terms</h2>
    <p>For a copy downloaded from Apple's App Store, <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a> applies unless the store listing provides an applicable custom license. These service terms do not replace that license or override mandatory consumer rights.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>The <a href={`${base}apps/chickubo/privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a> explains device and Apple/iCloud saves, support messages, optional Supabase account authentication and RevenueCat purchase verification, and account deletion. A purchase account does not back up or synchronize your farm.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Disclaimers and your rights</h2>
    <p>The game is provided "as is" and "as available" to the extent permitted by applicable law. To the extent the law allows, NekoCode is not responsible for indirect or consequential losses arising from use of the game. Nothing here excludes liability or consumer protections that cannot legally be excluded.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Updates and contact</h2>
    <p>You may stop using the game at any time. We may update these terms as the game changes and will post the revised date on this page. For questions or help, email <a href="mailto:nekocode.dev@gmail.com?subject=Chickubo%20Support">nekocode.dev@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</ChickuboInfoLayout>
